{
  "rationale": "Use a small plant split into sensing and motion capability, then encode the exploration and obstacle-recovery policy in compact deterministic specifications. The policy gives strong forward bias in clear space, uses one-shot short turns for side obstacles, uses brief backward escape only for front blockage, and reserves full_rotate for a dedicated repeated-failure last-resort path.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate uncontrollable perception from controllable motion capability in G",
    "Use one policy specification with perception states and one-shot action states so each non-decision state enables exactly one controllable action",
    "Bias clear-space behavior toward move_forward, allow occasional random_walk, and force obstacle events through recovery states",
    "Use move_backward only in dedicated front-obstacle recovery and full_rotate only from a dedicated stuck state after repeated blocked conditions"
  ],
